    {
      "source_id": "bg-openfinance-v2-protocol-functions",
      "locator": "page:95",
      "status": "resolved",
      "document": {
        "title": "openFinance Implementation Guidelines - Protocol Functions and Security Measures 2.3 (2025-10-31)",
        "kind": "pdf",
        "version": "openfinance-v2",
        "authority": "normative",
        "precedence": 100,
        "sha256": "323d2484a9cb08a8e657699180557244843f74605bdeec16349654114d5aa851",
        "status": "indexed"
      },
      "excerpt": "Security Measures supported by XS2A and openFinance API\n\n\nAttribute Type\n\nASPSP-SCA- String\nApproach\n\n\n\n\n8.5 Embedded SCA Approach\n\nThe Embedded SCA Approach is defined as the scenario where all PSU credentials are\ntransmitted via the XS2A API resp. the openFinance API. PSU identification data are\ntransported using the related header parameters as defined in Section\nInitiation Request and Response, an authorisation sub-resource is either implicitly generated\nby the ASPSP or needs to be explicitly created by the API Client in a next step, cp. Section\n\nThe API calls to create an authorisation sub-resource as well as the API calls to transmit PSU\ncredentials to the related authorisation resource within an Embedded SCA Approach are\ndefined in Section 9.4 and Section\nindicated by related hyperlinks presented by the ASPSP before.\n\n8.6 Decoupled SCA Approach\n\nThe Decoupled SCA Approach differs from the Embedded SCA Approach by using an ASPSP\nauthentication app for the strong customer authentication and dynamic linking if applicable.\nThe app is used by the PSU also for authentication of transaction in the online channels. Since\nthe XS2A API resp. the openFinance API is not involved in this…",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "source_id": "bg-openfinance-v2-protocol-functions",
          "document_id": "bg-openfinance-v2-protocol-functions@323d2484a9cb",
          "version": "openfinance-v2",
          "kind": "pdf",
          "authority": "normative",
          "precedence": 100,
          "locator": "page:95",
          "sha256": "3c77d5e2775a09e4d7991e52cc61f0494a43b7c34bace106ae26df7558b96e9e",
          "document_sha256": "323d2484a9cb08a8e657699180557244843f74605bdeec16349654114d5aa851"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_id": "bg-openfinance-v2-consent-api",
