    {
      "source_id": "project-openfinance-v2-errata",
      "locator": "section:E-01",
      "status": "resolved",
      "document": {
        "title": "Project errata and clarifications on the openFinance v2 corpus",
        "kind": "text",
        "version": "openfinance-v2",
        "authority": "project",
        "precedence": 10,
        "sha256": "0526127db9e64ec84102c2472ddb7f6b8170e284ec73ac508a7ef28ac161d431",
        "status": "indexed"
      },
      "excerpt": "E-01 ASPSP-SCA-Approach value SIGNATURE missing from the OpenAPI enum\n\nProtocol Functions and Security Measures 2.3, section 8.4.2 (page 95), lists the values\nEMBEDDED, DECOUPLED, REDIRECT, ASPSP-CHANNEL and SIGNATURE for the ASPSP-SCA-Approach\nresponse header. Consent API 2.2 uses \"ASPSP-SCA-Approach: SIGNATURE\" in an example (page 32).\nThe header definitions in the Signing Basket 2.3, Consent 2.1 and PIS 2.3 OpenAPI files list\nSIGNATURE in the description, but their enum only contains EMBEDDED, DECOUPLED, REDIRECT and\nASPSP-CHANNEL.\n\nClarification: the PDF value list prevails. SIGNATURE is a valid ASPSP-SCA-Approach value;\nclients generated from the OpenAPI enum must tolerate it.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "source_id": "project-openfinance-v2-errata",
          "document_id": "project-openfinance-v2-errata@0526127db9e6",
          "version": "openfinance-v2",
          "kind": "text",
          "authority": "project",
          "precedence": 10,
          "locator": "chunk:project-openfinance-v2-errata:p1:c1",
          "sha256": "f61fbf5b2dc6599f89948614cf01a732dbd705e76cfaf0454af9775125bc5697",
          "document_sha256": "0526127db9e64ec84102c2472ddb7f6b8170e284ec73ac508a7ef28ac161d431"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
